<title>USA: Knickerbocker suspends debt conversion.</title>
<headline>Knickerbocker suspends debt conversion.</headline>
<dateline>RANCHO SANTA MARGARITA, Calif. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>L.L. Knickerbocker Co Inc said Thursday it had suspended conversion of its 7.0 percent convertible debentures, issued in a Regulation D private placement financing of $15.5 million.</p>
<p>The company said it is investigating recent trading activity that it believes is related to the conversion terms of the debenture financing.</p>
<p>It reported the suspension in a Form 8-K with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) and the National Association of Securities Dealers.</p>
<p>The company said it took the action to protect shareholders and debenture holders.</p>
</text>
